{"case_id":"T8045","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","configuration","state","input semantics"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["h2o_socketpool_target_create","h2o_socketpool_init_specific","h2o_balancer_create_rr","h2o_balancer_create_lc","parse_balancer","parse_backends","on_config_reverse_url","set_targets","selector","try_connect"],"reason":"H0 fuzzes only HTTP wire bytes against a statically initialized reverse proxy containing one default-configured target. S1 materially changes the socketpool/balancer API and introduces configuration-dependent, multi-target behavior: variable-length target configuration is copied through conf_len, target weights are pointer-backed, round-robin requires set_targets initialization, and proxy.reverse.url can select weighted round-robin or least-conn backends. None of those dimensions is derived from fuzz input or exercised by H0. Moreover, H0 still calls h2o_socketpool_target_create(&upstream, NULL) while S1 declares a required third conf_len argument, so H0 is not source-compatible with S1 as supplied.","evidence":["H0 calls h2o_socketpool_target_create(&upstream, NULL) and constructs exactly one target before h2o_socketpool_init_specific(..., targets, 1, NULL).","S1 declares h2o_socketpool_target_create(h2o_url_t *origin, h2o_socketpool_target_conf_t *lb_target_conf, size_t conf_len) and allocates then memcpy-copies conf_len bytes when lb_target_conf is non-NULL.","S1 changes h2o_socketpool_target_t::conf from an inline structure to h2o_socketpool_target_conf_t *conf, consumed by least_conn.c and roundrobin.c through conf->weight.","S1 adds h2o_balancer_callbacks_t::set_targets and makes round-robin set_targets allocate floor_next_target and calculate cumulative weights across target_len targets.","parse_balancer accepts round-robin and least-conn, while parse_backends parses backend mappings containing url and weight and creates targets using balancer->target_conf_len.","H0's LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput passes Data only to create_accepted as an HTTP/1 or HTTP/2 request; configuration, backend count, balancer type, weights, conf_len, and target lifecycle are fixed outside the fuzz input."],"recommended_action":"Update H0 for the three-argument h2o_socketpool_target_create API and add a configuration/API-level fuzz target that generates proxy.reverse.url scalar, sequence, and mapping forms; varies backend counts, URLs, weights, balancer types, and malformed nodes; initializes socket pools through both round-robin and least-conn; and exercises repeated selection, failed-target retries, set_targets, and target destruction under sanitizers."}
